 "researcher_notes": "New row in the expansion shape under the Horizon parent row P0201. P0201 ends in McHenry County, Illinois, and has no row for this project. Natural Gas Pipeline Company of America (NGPL) leases the new capacity; Horizon holds the pipeline and is the Owner here. The Federal Energy Regulatory Commission scoping notice in the Federal Register on 2026-09-25 (docket CP26-564) gives 11.5 miles of new pipe from Lake County, Illinois, to Kenosha County, Wisconsin, 185,000 dekatherms per day of added firm service for Wisconsin Electric Power Company, plus compression at stations in Lake, Livingston and Will Counties. Cost of $438.5 million comes from a trade press story on the August 2026 application, which also gives an in-service date of the fourth quarter of 2028. The Kenosha County website names the end point as the Town of Paris. DataCenter is left blank on purpose. None of these sources ties this pipeline to data centers. The Kenosha County page says a separate 4-mile pipeline by We Energies will serve the Red Oak Ridge power plant, and the plant is tied to Microsoft in other reporting. No source says the North Extension itself feeds that plant. Revisit if the FERC filing or a utility document names Red Oak Ridge. Pipeline diameter and the route are not published in the sources read. PipelineType and FIDStatus left blank. Owner spelling matches the ownership team style. NGPL is an existing entity if the ownership team wants it as a second company."
}